WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.060
pain. Um

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.739
crisis precipitates change. People

00:00:03.739 --> 00:00:06.780
telling ghost stories really really

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:10.220
scares me. I think I&#x27;m a victim. I think

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.180
you&#x27;re a victim. Everybody is telling

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.260
weird ghost stories and we&#x27;re getting

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.940
really high off of these ideas, but we

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:20.780
don&#x27;t have any clue about the

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.420
consequence. We don&#x27;t have, as in my

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.659
opinion, we do have the ability in

00:00:25.659 --> 00:00:29.019
controlled context to trace the effects

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:33.420
of our word of our of our rhetoric. We

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.940
don&#x27;t track exactly how these behaviors,

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.340
these influential ideas, these ghost

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.099
stories

00:00:41.099 --> 00:00:43.739
change people&#x27;s lives. Now, of course,

00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:45.900
we can always say everybody&#x27;s working as

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.060
hard as they can. They&#x27;re evolutionarily

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.739
fit beings trying to make the most of

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:52.620
their situations. So, we have a bit of

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.340
bias, survivorship bias, of saying, &quot;Oh,

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.299
we did fine with how this is. Why don&#x27;t

00:00:58.299 --> 00:01:02.300
we simply do what we know?&quot;
